From: Construct <release@constructlinux.org>
Subject: session: Stop a conversation's worker before closing its connection

stop_conversation() closed the worker's connection and then sent the
worker SIGTERM. A worker waiting on a query - gdm-password, for the
password of a prompt the person cancelled or the shell took down - saw
its query fail first, returned PAM_CONV_ERR to the module, and pam_unix
logged two errors for a prompt nobody failed:

  pam_unix(gdm-password:auth): conversation failed
  pam_unix(gdm-password:auth): auth could not identify password for [x]

A worker that has not started a session exits on SIGTERM at once
(session-worker-main.c, on_sigterm_cb), so sent first it is gone before
the query can fail. Its connection is closed after: a connection whose
peer is gone is closed already as GDBus sees it, refuses to close again
and keeps its socket until it is finalized, so the stream is closed by
hand - measured as one socket kept per prompt in the session's worker
otherwise.

--- a/daemon/gdm-session.c
+++ b/daemon/gdm-session.c
@@ -2425,7 +2425,10 @@
         if (conversation->worker_proxy != NULL) {
                 GDBusConnection *connection = g_dbus_proxy_get_connection (G_DBUS_PROXY (conversation->worker_proxy));
 
-                g_dbus_connection_close_sync (connection, NULL, NULL);
+                /* A connection the worker's exit closed already refuses to close again, and
+                 * keeps its socket until it is finalized: the stream is closed by hand. */
+                if (!g_dbus_connection_close_sync (connection, NULL, NULL))
+                        g_io_stream_close (g_dbus_connection_get_stream (connection), NULL, NULL);
         }
 
 }
@@ -2433,19 +2436,23 @@
 static void
 stop_conversation (GdmSessionConversation *conversation)
 {
-        close_conversation (conversation);
-
+        /* The worker first: a worker that has not started a session exits on
+         * SIGTERM at once, where closing its connection first makes the query
+         * it is waiting on fail, and the PAM module log the cancelled
+         * conversation as an error before the signal reaches it. */
         conversation->is_stopping = TRUE;
         gdm_session_worker_job_stop (conversation->job);
+
+        close_conversation (conversation);
 }
 
 static void
 stop_conversation_now (GdmSessionConversation *conversation)
 {
-        close_conversation (conversation);
-
         gdm_session_worker_job_stop_now (conversation->job);
         g_clear_object (&conversation->job);
+
+        close_conversation (conversation);
 }
 
 void
